# SG-6's flash check (tests/e2e/glitch.py) through a quick look up and back down, booted on 0020
# facing north: the move that showed the pink horizon for a frame when VDP2's planes were one frame
# ahead of VDP1's picture (jo before johannes-fetz/joengine#111; src/view.c VDP2_PLANE_DELAY). Every frame is recorded and checked, so the fault
# is found without a shot having to land on it. The holes check needs the magenta back colour, so
# run_e2e.ps1 builds this film with GLITCH_CHECK on
record
boot_at 0020
wait_up
wait 1.0
hold left 0.6
wait 1.0
flashes_from
holes_from
wait 0.3
keydown y
wait 0.6
keyup y
wait 0.6
flashes_to look_up
holes_to look_up
shot flash_00_end
